<https://github.com/john1hsu/aws-graph/id/cell-based-architecture> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A resilience pattern that splits a workload into multiple isolated, identical, fixed-size copies called cells, each serving a subset of customers chosen by a partition key behind a thin cell router, so that a failure, bad deployment or poison-pill request is contained to one cell rather than the whole fleet." .
