<https://github.com/john1hsu/aws-graph/id/edge-locations> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "AWS edge locations (points of presence) are a globally distributed network of sites, separate from Regions and Availability Zones, that host edge services such as Amazon CloudFront, Amazon Route 53 and AWS Global Accelerator close to end users and connect back to Regions over the AWS backbone." .
