<https://github.com/john1hsu/aws-graph/id/eks-auto-mode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An Amazon EKS operating mode in which AWS also runs the cluster's data plane: it launches, scales, patches and retires EC2 worker nodes through Karpenter-style NodePools and NodeClasses, and supplies built-in networking, load balancing and storage, for a per-instance management fee." .
