<https://github.com/john1hsu/aws-graph/id/fips-140-3-on-aws> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "How AWS meets the U.S./Canadian FIPS 140-3 standard for cryptographic modules: services rely on CMVP-validated modules (AWS-LC, the AWS KMS and CloudHSM HSMs, Nitro engines), and customers who need FIPS-validated TLS in transit must opt in to FIPS endpoints, which exist only in U.S., GovCloud (US) and Canadian Regions." .
