<https://github.com/john1hsu/aws-graph/id/shuffle-sharding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A fault-isolation pattern in which each customer or resource is assigned its own pseudo-random combination of workers (a virtual \"shuffle shard\") instead of one fixed shard, so a poison-pill request or flood aimed at one customer degrades only its combination while other customers keep at least some healthy workers." .
